--TEST--
A piece of `Core\IO::stdinStream` is `tainted bytes`, so a loop variable declared as plain `bytes` does not compile — `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\IO::stdinStream
// Standard input comes from outside the program, so every piece is tainted.
foreach (Core\IO::stdinStream() as bytes $piece) {
    echo Core\Bytes::length($piece), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `bytes`, found `tainted bytes`
%A
